# --- Non-Unity tooling & planning artifacts ---
# The BMad framework itself is installed tooling — reinstallable, so not tracked.
/_bmad/
# Its OUTPUT is not: the GDD, epics, story files and sprint status are the design
# record of this project. They are not needed to *build* it, but they are the least
# reproducible thing in the repo — months of decisions with no other history. Tracked.
# Only verification output is excluded: that is evidence produced by a test run
# (9MB+ of PNGs per story), not source, and it is regenerated by re-running the rig.
/_bmad-output/verification/
# Claude Code: CLAUDE.md is versioned on purpose — it holds project knowledge (Jira
# sync contract, verification expectations, Unity traps already paid for), not personal
# preferences, so it belongs with the code. Same reasoning applies to settings.json:
# it is the project's shared permission allowlist, so it is tracked. Everything else
# under .claude/ stays local — settings.local.json is personal, and skills/ is 4.2MB
# of BMad-installed tooling that the installer regenerates.
/.claude/*
!/.claude/settings.json
!/.claude/hooks/
# Agent definitions (BMad/GDS agents authored under .github/agents — not GitHub Actions CI)
/.agents/
/.github/agents/
# Source/staging art — raw Blender (.blend) + master FBX + concept doc.
# These are the SOURCE files; the pieces actually used get imported into Assets/
# (which IS tracked). Kept out of git on purpose: the 214MB "game map .blend"
# exceeds GitHub's 100MB per-file limit. Version source art via Git LFS or external
# storage if it ever needs tracking.
/CAMERA GAME SHARED FOLDER/

# Unity crash-recovery backups (auto-created after an unexpected shutdown; not real content)
/Assets/_Recovery/
/Assets/_Recovery.meta
